  {
   "role": "agent",
   "text": "Thanks, Maya. You're verified.\n\nYour Pho Real order (O-5101) was promised by 6:40 PM and arrived at 7:05 PM, which is 25 minutes late. I've added **$3.99** in account credit, equal to your delivery fee. You can use it on a future order.\n\nI'm sorry the pho was lukewarm. Our policy doesn't allow a refund or credit for food temperature, so I can't offer anything more for that. The pho wasn't missing or wrong, and you didn't report a food-safety problem.\n\nIs there anything else I can help with?"
  },
  {
   "role": "customer",
   "text": "Hold on, $3.99 in credit for a 25-minute delay and cold food? I paid for dinner and I'd like the money back on my Visa, not app credit I might never use."
  },
  {
   "role": "agent",
   "text": "I understand the frustration, Maya. I'm still not able to refund this to your Visa. Under our policy, late deliveries are compensated with account credit only, never a refund to the card. A 25-minute delay falls in the tier that earns a credit equal to the delivery fee, which is the $3.99 I've already applied.\n\nLukewarm food isn't a reason we can refund or credit for. A refund would only apply if an item was missing or wrong, and that doesn't seem to be the case here.\n\nIf you'd like a person to review your case, I can pass it to a specialist, who would follow up within 24 hours. I can't promise what they'd decide. Would you like me to do that, or is there anything else I can help with?"
  },
  {
   "role": "customer",
   "text": "Okay. I'm not thrilled, but I'm too tired to fight about it tonight. Fine, I'll take the credit. I don't want a specialist follow-up."
  }
